course: dictionary
lesson: 7614
title: Privately: in secret, alone, or owned
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Privately is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done. Its main meaning is without other people being there or knowing, or in secret. «Correcting a teacher privately instead of in front of everyone is kind and is usually welcomed.» The clue is «instead of in front of everyone»: privately means the opposite of in front of everyone.
explain: Privately can also mean in your own thoughts, not said out loud. In «privately, she was scared», she may look calm, but nobody has heard her say it, so the fear is hidden inside her.
explain: Privately can describe something owned by a person or company, not the government: «a privately owned park». When you meet privately, swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Privately means without other people being there or knowing, or in secret or alone.
fact: «Privately» can also mean in your own thoughts, not said out loud.
fact: «Privately owned» means owned by a person or company, not by the government.
fact: «Speak privately» means talk to someone with just the two of you, away from others.
fact: Telling a trusted adult or teacher about a worry in private is a safe and sensible choice.
exercise: «Correcting a teacher privately instead of in front of everyone is kind.» What does privately mean here? | *Without everyone else there to see | Very quickly | Loudly, so the whole class can hear | On the teacher's own desk
exercise: «Privately, she was scared.» What does privately mean here? | Owned by a company | Shouting in a crowd | *In her own thoughts, not said out loud | Paid for by the government
exercise: Find the phrase where privately means owned by a person or company, not the government. | a private joke shared by two friends | *a privately owned park | speak quietly in class | a secret handshake
test: What does privately mean in «speak privately to a teacher about a worry»? | *Without other people listening | Happily, with a big smile | Quickly, before lunch | Very loudly in the hall
test: In «many people paid privately for dentists», what does paid privately mean? | Paid nothing at all | Paid in a loud voice in the shop | Paid with coins from the ground | *Paid for by themselves, not by the NHS
exam: Which sentence uses privately to mean in your own thoughts? | Mia spoke privately with her friend in the corridor. | The park was privately owned by a family. | *He thought privately that the plan was silly, but he kept quiet. | They went to the dentist privately last week.
